      "writtenOn": "2017-04-26T01:00:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which would you prefer for the enqueue case if I switch to a single list lock per proc:\n\n1) specify the proc to use for the list lock as an argument (NULL would mean locking is done externally):\n\n  binder_enqueue_work(proc, \u0026node-\u003ework, target_list);\n\nor\n\n2) abandon the enqueue/dequeue wrappers which means they would look like:\n\n  spin_lock(\u0026proc-\u003elist_lock);\n  list_add_tail(\u0026node-\u003ework.entry, target_list);\n  spin_unlock(\u0026proc-\u003elist_lock);\n\n(I prefer #1 of these)",
